/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Benchmark D -- topology: methanol from CO2, the plant as the reference
  sample wires it.  Stream names are the sample's "MSTR-0nn" numbers with
  an `s` prefix (s40 = MSTR-040); the named streams keep their names
  (hydrogen, co2Feed, cw1..cw3, purge, vent, waterProduct, methanolProduct).
  Unit names are the sample's tags shortened (COMP-005 -> C5, HE-012 ->
  HX12, SEP-051 -> SEP51, SC-085 -> COL85, VALV-058 -> V58, PUMP-066 -> P66,
  MIX-037 -> M37, SPLT-057 -> SPLIT57).

   hydrogen ─► C5 (to 78 bar) ─► s6 ─┐
   co2Feed ─► C10 (3 bar) ─► HX12 ─► C16 (8.8 bar) ─► HX19 ─► C23 (26.3 bar) ─► HX26 ─► C27 (78 bar) ─► s31 ─┤
                 cw1 ─┘ s14         cw2 ─┘ s21           cw3 ─┘ s30                                 M37 ─► s33 ─┐
                                                                                                               │
          ┌───────────────────── s44 (recycle, heated) ──────────────────────────────────────────────── M39 ◄──┘
          │                                                                                        (510.15 K)  │ s40
          │  HX41 cold ◄── s43 ◄── SPLIT57 (0.56) ◄── s55 ◄── V54 (73 bar) ◄── s52 ◄── SEP51 (vapour) ◄── s46 ◄── PC45 (vf 0.9) ◄── s42 ◄── HX41 hot ◄── sPFR ◄── PFR (20 m3, 510.15 K)
          └──────────────────────┘              │ purge (0.44)          │ s53 (liquid)
                                                                        ▼
                                  V58 (10 bar) ─► s61 ─► V59 (1 atm) ─► s62 ─► SEP62 ─► vent (vapour)
                                                                                 │ s64 (liquid)
                                                                                 ▼
                                   P66 (to 2 bar) ─► s67 ─► V67 (to 1 atm) ─► s67a ─► COL85 ─► waterProduct (bottoms)
                                                                                         │ s70 (distillate)
                                                                                         ▼
                                                                                 COL78 ─► methanolProduct (distillate), s80 (bottoms)

  THE WORKAROUNDS, each stated (README has the list with its reason):
    1. The sample's PFR runs in its "outlet temperature" mode (489.0 K in,
       510.15 K out, -96.3 kW).  Vitor's decision (DEV.md 4c C123): the
       reactor is ISOTHERMAL at that outlet temperature.  Choupo's `pfr`
       takes its isothermal T from its FEED, so the reactor-feed mixer M39
       DECLARES 510.15 K and publishes the duty that implies (the mixer's
       isothermal form, docs/ai/unit-ops.md); the reactor's own duty is the
       isothermal heat of reaction.  Their sum is compared with the sample's
       -96.3 kW.
    2. The sample's HE-045 condenses the effluent to a vapour fraction of
       0.9 against cooling water (its U is computed from that spec).
       Choupo's `phaseChanger` with `outletQuality 0.9` lands the same
       outlet; the cooling-water side is not in this flowsheet and the duty
       is compared as a number (the sample's CW4 outlet is in `reference`).
    3. The sample's recycle compressor COMP-054 (7299999.99996 Pa ->
       7300000 Pa, stored work -0.00122 kW) does no work, but it is NOT a
       no-op: its 73 bar outlet FIXES THE LOOP PRESSURE, because the
       sample's mixers take the minimum inlet pressure and the 78 bar
       make-up meets the 73 bar recycle in MIX-039.  (A first mapping that
       omitted it ran the loop at the make-up's 78 bar; measured, that
       moved the reactor outlet's methanol by +14 %.)  A Choupo compressor
       refuses P_out <= P_in, so a VALVE V54 to 73 bar stands in its place:
       at convergence it drops nothing, and Choupo's mixer takes the
       minimum inlet pressure too, so the loop runs at 73 bar as the
       sample's does.
    4. The sample's VALV-083 (101325 Pa -> 101325 Pa) is a no-op and is
       omitted: COL78 reads COL85's distillate directly.
    5. Choupo's `shortcutColumn` runs at its FEED's pressure; the sample's
       pump discharges at 2 bar into a column at 1 atm.  A let-down valve
       V67 to 1 atm sits between pump and column.
    6. The sample fixes each shortcut column by the light key's mole
       fraction in the bottoms and the heavy key's in the distillate (0.01 /
       0.01; 0.1 / 0.001); Choupo's takes RECOVERIES.  The recoveries below
       are the sample's own stored product balances: COL85 LK 0.986955, HK
       0.007702; COL78 LK 0.998967, HK 0.098992 (README shows the arithmetic).
    7. The sample's hydrogen feed is stored two-phase (vapour fraction
       0.9656 at 298 K, 10.75 bar: its 3.7 % water condenses) and its
       compressor is set to ignore the phase.  Choupo's compressor computes
       on the vapour root of the overall composition and says nothing; the
       energy report, which resolves the feed, then finds 24.93 kW at C5
       that no term accounts for -- a Choupo finding (README), not the same
       reading as the sample's, which was the first draft of this note.

  THERMODYNAMICS: constant/thermoPhysPropDict (PR78, the E-PPR78 set at
  510.15 K, the three regressed methanol pairs).  Every unit inherits it.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    // ---- hydrogen compression ----------------------------------------------
    {
        name        C5;
        type        compressor;
        in          hydrogen;
        outputs     ( s6 );
        operation   { P_out 7800000 Pa;  eta 0.75; }
    }

    // ---- CO2 compression train, three water intercoolers ------------------
    {
        name        C10;
        type        compressor;
        in          co2Feed;
        outputs     ( s11 );
        operation   { P_out 300000 Pa;  eta 0.75; }
    }
    {
        name        HX12;
        type        heatExchanger;
        inputs      ( s11  cw1 );
        outputs     ( s15  s14 );
        operation   { area 1 m2;  U 1000 W/m2/K;  flow counter; }
    }
    {
        name        C16;
        type        compressor;
        in          s15;
        outputs     ( s17 );
        operation   { P_out 880000 Pa;  eta 0.75; }
    }
    {
        name        HX19;
        type        heatExchanger;
        inputs      ( s17  cw2 );
        outputs     ( s22  s21 );
        operation   { area 1 m2;  U 1000 W/m2/K;  flow counter; }
    }
    {
        name        C23;
        type        compressor;
        in          s22;
        outputs     ( s24 );
        operation   { P_out 2630000 Pa;  eta 0.75; }
    }
    {
        name        HX26;
        type        heatExchanger;
        inputs      ( s24  cw3 );
        outputs     ( s28  s30 );
        operation   { area 1 m2;  U 1000 W/m2/K;  flow counter; }
    }
    {
        name        C27;
        type        compressor;
        in          s28;
        outputs     ( s31 );
        operation   { P_out 7800000 Pa;  eta 0.75; }
    }
    {
        name        M37;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( s31  s6 );
        outputs     ( s33 );
    }

    // ---- the synthesis loop (tears: s40, s43) ------------------------------
    {
        name        PFR;
        type        pfr;
        in          s40;
        outputs     ( sPFR );
        operation
        {
            V_R              20 m3;          // the sample's reactor volume
            nSteps           5000;           // RK4 steps: 200 overshot CO2 to zero near the inlet on the first pass (the rate law then has no value); a numerical aid, stated
            thermalMode      isothermal;     // at the feed's 510.15 K (workaround 1)
            catalystLoading  1153.87;        // kg/m3, the sample's value (= VBF Table 3's 1775 kg/m3 pellets at 0.35 bed voidage)
        }
        reactions   ( methanolSynthesis  rwgs );   // constant/reactions: Vanden Bussche & Froment 1996
    }
    {
        name        HX41;
        type        heatExchanger;
        inputs      ( sPFR  s43 );
        outputs     ( s42  s44 );
        operation   { area 1 m2;  U 1000 W/m2/K;  flow counter; }
    }
    {
        name        PC45;
        type        phaseChanger;
        in          s42;
        outputs     ( s46 );
        operation   { outletQuality 0.9; }   // workaround 2: the sample's hot-side spec
    }
    {
        name        SEP51;
        type        isothermalFlash;
        in          s46;
        outputs     ( s53  s52 );
        operation   { }                      // separates the feed at its own (T, P)
    }
    {
        name        V54;
        type        valve;
        in          s52;
        outputs     ( s55 );
        operation   { P 7300000 Pa; }        // workaround 3: COMP-054's outlet, the loop pressure
    }
    {
        name        SPLIT57;
        type        splitter;
        in          s55;
        outputs     ( purge  s43 );
        operation   { fractions ( 0.44  0.56 ); }   // the sample's split ratios
    }
    {
        name        M39;
        type        mixer;
        inputs      ( s33  s44 );
        outputs     ( s40 );
        operation   { T 510.15 K; }          // workaround 1: the reactor's isothermal T is its feed's
    }

    // ---- let-down, vent flash, pump, the two columns -------------------------
    {
        name        V58;
        type        valve;
        in          s53;
        outputs     ( s61 );
        operation   { P 1000000 Pa; }
    }
    {
        name        V59;
        type        valve;
        in          s61;
        outputs     ( s62 );
        operation   { P 101325 Pa; }
    }
    {
        name        SEP62;
        type        isothermalFlash;
        in          s62;
        outputs     ( s64  vent );
        operation   { }
    }
    {
        name        P66;
        type        pump;
        in          s64;
        outputs     ( s67 );
        operation   { eta 0.75;  P_out 200000 Pa; }
    }
    {
        name        V67;
        type        valve;
        in          s67;
        outputs     ( s67a );
        operation   { P 101325 Pa; }         // workaround 5: the column runs at its feed's P
    }
    {
        name        COL85;
        type        shortcutColumn;
        in          s67a;
        outputs     ( s70  waterProduct );
        operation
        {
            lightKey      methanol;
            heavyKey      water;
            recoveryLK    0.986955;          // workaround 6: the sample's own balance
            recoveryHK    0.007702;
            refluxRatio   1.5;
        }
    }
    {
        name        COL78;
        type        shortcutColumn;
        in          s70;
        outputs     ( methanolProduct  s80 );
        operation
        {
            lightKey      methanol;
            heavyKey      water;
            recoveryLK    0.998967;
            recoveryHK    0.098992;
            refluxRatio   1.5;
        }
    }
);
